    "source": "1820 census at the census date, free adult men outside the Southern states; the census gives free white males 16\u201318, 18\u201326, 26\u201345 and 45+, so men 21+ are split from the 18\u201326 band. Voters were men meeting each state's rules: several states still required property or taxpaying qualifications (Virginia and Rhode Island a freehold). Electors were chosen by popular vote in 15 states; elsewhere (Alabama, Delaware, Georgia, Indiana, Louisiana, Missouri, New York, South Carolina and Vermont) men cast no presidential vote. Free Black men could vote in some Northern states on the same or stricter terms."
