    "source": "1820 census at the census date, Black adults in Virginia, North Carolina, South Carolina, Georgia, Tennessee, Louisiana, Mississippi and Alabama; the census gives free people of colour and enslaved people by sex and age band. The great majority were enslaved and could not vote. Free Black men meeting the property tests could legally vote only in North Carolina (until its 1835 constitution) and Tennessee (until its 1834 constitution); the other Southern states limited the vote to white men. In South Carolina, Georgia, Louisiana and Alabama the legislature chose the electors, so no one there voted for president directly."
   }
